@page "/object-explorer"
@attribute [Authorize]

@*
    The Object Explorer landing page. This routable shell renders statically
    so its <PageTitle> reaches the (static-SSR) HeadOutlet and lands in the
    HTML response as a real <title> - the browser tab is right on the first
    paint and on enhanced navigation, before any circuit exists.

    The list itself is interactive and lives in ReleasesBrowserView, rendered
    with prerender:false. Under default InteractiveServer the body rendered
    twice (SSR pass with data, then the circuit re-ran OnInitializedAsync from
    a blank state), which flashed the list back to "Loading...". A
    PersistentComponentState bridge (PR #507) fixed the flash but destabilised
    the circuit in production - dead tabs on first load, circuit shutdowns on
    navigation. Skipping prerender is the same trade OeReleaseDetail makes:
    the first paint is the loading state, the data loads exactly once, and no
    persistence machinery rides on the live circuit.

    Putting the title on a static shell is what OeReleaseDetail can't do - its
    title is the release label, which only exists once the interactive body has
    loaded, so that page sets document.title from JS instead. This one's title
    is a constant, so it belongs in the response.
*@

<PageTitle>Object Explorer · AL Dev Toolbox</PageTitle>

<ReleasesBrowserView @rendermode="@(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))" />
